text(await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_create_pull_request({repository_full_name:"sundial-org/sun",base:"main",head:"codex/group-history-by-turn",title:"Group Sun log and viz history by session turn",body:"Interleaved agent edits can prevent Git squashing, leaving individual tool calls as separate rows in `sun log` and `sun viz`. Group those display rows by actor, session, turn, and branch while retaining the underlying commits and per-operation snapshots. Terminal and HTML details expose the constituent snapshots, and `-n` limits complete display entries. `sun data` continues to expose raw commits.

Initialize missing turn state on the first tool call so subagents without a UserPromptSubmit hook receive numbered turns. Existing `turn0` records remain separate because their boundaries are unknown.

Validation: ran the 210-test regression suite; 209 passed, with one failure in an earlier version of the new test that saved HTML inside its test repository. Corrected that fixture to use an external output path. All five focused checks then passed, covering interleaved turns, raw-history preservation, legacy turn0 records, Codex subagent boundaries, and terminal/HTML output. `git diff --check` passed.",draft:false}));

